A||||6||bya72||how do you get the luggage rack off?||||1||
Z||000000||bya72||06-19-2001||04:15 PM||||I am geting the car preped to be painted.  I want to take the luggage rack off and sand the deck down.  Do the trim pieces on the top have to come off first?  Or is there another way to do it so I don't trash them?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||06-19-2001||04:52 PM||||You have to carefully remove the strips in the center of the rails.  They just pull out.  Then you'll see the screws that attatch the rails to  the decklid.  There is one nut underneath the decklid at each end of the "spoiler" that need to come off too. After you have removed the rack you can remove the bolt anchors from the holes in the decklid with a small screwdriver.  They are rubber "plugs" and will come out giving you a nice flat surface that is easy to sand.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||06-20-2001||12:07 PM||||then fill the holes in and throw the luggage rack away - they sure are ugly - I cant wait to get rid of mine!<P>  too much like a subaru outback<P>  I dont think I have ever seen a ferrari with a luggage rack, or a porche<p>[This message has been edited by Ken Wittlief (edited 06-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero5||06-20-2001||08:41 PM||||Tha fastest and easiest way I have found is get a replacement deck lid without the rack stuff. As a bonus, if you get one the same color in great shape you are golden. In your case as it is getting painted anyway, color may not matter.<P>Steve<P>------------------<BR>                              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pegasuscolors_sig_copy.jpg">  <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||12
Z||000004||bya72||06-20-2001||09:36 PM||||I would love to get a new deck.  But it is more of a cost issue right now.  Trying to buy a house, redo the Fiero, get more mods for the Jeep is hard to do on a teacher's salary.  All that is left on the Jeep is big ticket items so I am turning my attention to the Fiero.  Found a friend who will paint it for about 100 bucks plus paint.  I can't beat that deal, I just have to do all the prep.  Tomorrow I am going to try to take the luggage rack off.  I haven't decided if I am going to leave it off or not.  Thanks for the help.||||reg||1
